^SIGNAL=0$
--
^PARSING ERROR$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
std::variant<int, double> with libc++: holds_alternative and get of the
held int.  It depends on the expansion of a using-declaration pack, braced
initialization of an array-reference parameter and constant evaluation in
libc++'s <variant>.  It also guards against a partially type-checked main:
an incomplete user function is an error, not a SUCCESSFUL result over a
truncated body (see test.desc).
